d{aligned}].$\n\n- Since $A$ is lower-triangular, the eigenvalues are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=-3\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=2.\n$$\n\n- Let's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors.\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=-3,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{1}I=[\\begin{aligned}5 & 0 \\\\ -6 & 0\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=2,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{2}I=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ -6 & -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}].$\n\nNow, we write down the general solution to the given linear system of differential equations: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-3t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -6\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-327974/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9cfc838b-2e21-5021-8afc-000d12acdf39"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-327974"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} [:db/retract 17592186129522 :question/answer-fields 17592186126926] {:db/id "q-324453/selection/ma-v1/2b830b818b7c8c122c889f4df99bebc494520819e3d5b3be7f072591fc9b8d82/84c6c5a8ad3bd889927e0990cafba18266f7b85c030d55a5d5dbf46c2bd19461" :answer/id #uuid "310a8d85-f17b-58b7-8c55-bb995adeca16" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-2t},\\,{c}_{1}\\in R" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-324453/selection/ma-v1/2b830b818b7c8c122c889f4df99bebc494520819e3d5b3be7f072591fc9b8d82/4765682070e348c2e5d1d7ac0fe123ce639ac7eda4d5dbd4bc9cae3d8202007b" :answer/id #uuid "599e93ee-258b-50be-8b5b-83ece2e686b8" :answer/type :answer.type