ot 2-(-1)\\cdot (-3)}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-79710/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2a962d5e-5cc9-530e-9f95-85c399af7e4b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-79710"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-327999/selection/9aa19eecefd76848ec59ecc2f8f9dcebebb69f08cd99d43893dca6de121858bf" :answer/id #uuid "826d5ec3-0fbb-51ca-98ce-94136c26a92f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)=-{u}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)={u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327999/selection/ee464a5eaa57e341c9c89b33b42e3fc7ac0062786acd098b4a0df985e3151c36" :answer/id #uuid "bfa64c7d-e1d2-540b-ba93-6ce59a84b434" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)=-{u}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)={u}_{1}(t)-{u}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327999/selection/25ba00fe6f85df1dbb469aef16bf4abc3a6eae44ce5be519ed3b85d52df9f61a" :answer/id #uuid "39cd13ca-b0e2-511b-a50a-a40be01e5e50" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)=-{u}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)=-{u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327999/selection/4d28da51d07ea54e403172975beda5a5c74dcc6df1a9e3d5582793831bdf1f10" :answer/id #uuid "4298549d-f15e-5e96-b7a9-80c328d38381" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)=-{u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)={u}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327999/selection/255b2b8acbb8f4e26e0c021205fa9d2bcd9b12b2bf75d63256e14cfaec7381cc" :answer/id #uuid "2692c169-681b-5cd1-816e-d524e5e82979" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)={u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)={u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327999/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "ffd7b197-a9e0-56a3-a34d-eda7c0d54092" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-327999/selection/9aa19eecefd76848ec59ecc2f8f9dcebebb69f08cd99d43893dca6de121858bf" :answer-field/choices ["q-327999/selection/9aa19eecefd76848ec59ecc2f8f9dcebebb69f08cd99d43893dca6de121858bf" "q-327999/selection/ee464a5eaa57e341c9c89b33b42e3fc7ac0062786acd098b4a0df985e3151c36" "q-327999/selection/25ba00fe6f85df1dbb469aef16bf4abc3a6eae44ce5be519ed3b85d52df9f61a" "q-327999/selection/4d28da51d07ea54e403172975beda5a5c74dcc6df1a9e3d5582793831bdf1f10" "q-327999/selection/255b2b8acbb8f4e26e0c021205fa9d2bcd9b12b2bf75d63256e14cfaec7381cc"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-327999" :question/id #uuid "88f4bcdc-08ae-5cd3-83e3-4ae7b98eda2d" :question/math-academy-id "q-327999" :question/problem "Find the substitution that will decouple the following system of differential equations: \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-3{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t)-2{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- Since $A$ is lower-triangular, the eigenvalues are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=-3\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=-2.\n$$\n\n- Let's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors.\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=-3,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{1}I=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=-2,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{2}I=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nTherefore, we have $E=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nFinally, the change of variables that decouples the system is given by $x(t)=Eu(t)$, or equivalently,\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)=-{u}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)={u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-327999/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2a962d5e-5cc9-530e-9f95-85c399af7e4b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-327999"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-327997/selection/a25b1efac038e9a61e7f3c410c4ddbdd2057b9784482c44a45a2b6e936ae2ce3" :answer/id #uuid "fee110ee-6556-59ed-8d10-a55791b654b5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)=-{u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)={u}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327997/selection/d7ca297b82eb629b65a6baab347152601a24ce9dff8d624c9014923f1a3dcda5" :answer/id #uuid "a6b51f3c-8225-583c-8cce-232156a59797" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)=-{u}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)={u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327997/selection/5de56cc09955695a8c82ace97e82914d3c12d356bb961fc104ffdf5e54365ab8" :answer/id #uuid "36c8f169-d1a5-59a4-8b2e-8e973aaf3d8e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)={u}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)={u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327997/selection/6f73001774da950cd83c2f20dfe7eec4be1b9b801bad53ff9b8d3a3aaf292996" :answer/id #uuid "1cffb798-db0a-5a84-9d2b-629e407a7d27" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)={u}_{1}(t)-{u}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)={u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327997/selection/134df696e749ee558b2ad668fd8a030704b13dcac955b73da4ad0bd8985641dd" :answer/id #uuid "c65d59ff-12bd-53c0-aaa0-9321c981191c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)=-{u}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)={u}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327997/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "aa6e2baa-8a1e-5418-bb23-7a1c54ecd2d1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-327997/selection/d7ca297b82eb629b65a6baab347152601a24ce9dff8d624c9014923f1a3dcda5" :answer-field/choices ["q-327997/selection/a25b1efac038e9a61e7f3c410c4ddbdd2057b9784482c44a45a2b6e936ae2ce3" "q-327997/selection/d7ca297b82eb629b65a6baab347152601a24ce9dff8d624c9014923f1a3dcda5" "q-327997/selection/5de56cc09955695a8c82ace97e82914d3c12d356bb961fc104ffdf5e54365ab8" "q-327997/selection/6f73001774da950cd83c2f20dfe7eec4be1b9b801bad53ff9b8d3a3aaf292996" "q-327997/selection/134df696e749ee558b2ad668fd8a030704b13dcac955b73da4ad0bd8985641dd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-327997" :question/id #uuid "5f0bc18c-9cad-5fa9-b040-3bff4cc9faa5" :question/math-academy-id "q-327997" :question/problem "Find the substitution that will decouple the following system of differential equations: \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)={x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-2{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- Since $A$ is lower-triangular, the eigenvalues are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=1\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=-1.\n$$\n\n- Let's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors.\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=1,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{1}I=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & -2\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=-1,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{2}I=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nTherefore, we have $E=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, the change of variables that decouples the system is given by $x(t)=Eu(t)$, or equivalently,\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)=-{u}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)={u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-327997/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2a962d5e-5cc9-530e-9f95-85c399af7e4b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-327997"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-39699/selection/ff3569f7c50814c64c3778602e6704c9cd27be8fbca8f408198dcaaed7ca7d58" :answer/id #uuid "709f9a42-56e4-5889-aa47-da5d98b00cc0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39699/selection/8c09129001253dc72c82e11ccd9b2ca72d0996993fc92b4e746f757044b81cf8" :answer/id #uuid "4b30e091-5ef6-5b9c-817a-19be1a86f57c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39699/selection/d76648267380385323cccd6e0da16d9c296d8cebe6b6fba28614bad6f2dee74e" :answer/id #uuid "87f69981-7b79-5845-870b-409559b440a6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39699/selection/291bdf039e4b6905ebee91262158193966fd21a4f3022edcc506e034e482127e" :answer/id #uuid "71830596-5160-5f30-abf6-2ebce447c516" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39699/selection/b6f02be0235b89d54b40b2f4b7200cc2eb45559eab2c2d2de78b4d51a3eb92cd" :answer/id #uuid "1cd77233-04e1-5b99-a546-a947864d2dc5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -2\\end{aligned}]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-39699/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d443d88f-d41e-5f52-8174-d04982c0be18" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-39699/selection/ff3569f7c50814c64c3778602e6704c9cd27be8fbca8f408198dcaaed7ca7d58" :answer-field/choices ["q-39699/selection/ff3569f7c50814c64c3778602e6704c9cd27be8fbca8f408198dcaaed7ca7d58" "q-39699/selection/8c09129001253dc72c82e11ccd9b2ca72d0996993fc92b4e746f757044b81cf8" "q-39699/selection/d76648267380385323cccd6e0da16d9c296d8cebe6b6fba28614bad6f2dee74e" "q-39699/selection/291bdf039e4b6905ebee91262158193966fd21a4f3022edcc506e034e482127e" "q-39699/selection/b6f02be0235b89d54b40b2f4b7200cc2eb45559eab2c2d2de78b4d51a3eb92cd"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-39699" :question/id #uuid "547cf423-346c-5ea7-9462-268138005651" :question/math-academy-id "q-39699" :question/problem "Let ${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ and ${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ be eigenvectors of a matrix $A.$ Find the decoupling matrix of the differential equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we construct the matrix $E$, whose columns are the eigenvectors ${v}_{1}$ and ${v}_{2}:$\n\n$$\nE=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nNow, the decoupling matrix can be found as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & ={E}^{-1} \\\\  & ={[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ -2 & -1\\end{aligned}]}^{-1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot (-1)-1\\cdot (-2)}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-39699/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2a962d5e-5cc9-530e-9f95-85c399af7e4b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-39699"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-327995/selection/ea592d2b5df637fe876c4088b48c3bd8c43a23710531534f1b801de5b7751ea3" :answer/id #uuid "10d5a617-ae80-54b3-a57d-a4e0bf311386" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)=-{u}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)={u}_{1}(t)-{u}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327995/selection/fd562ba3a6d9d1e8c9739c1ce8f9fc0339e036fa8ea4ccfedc638fcf9b06c956" :answer/id #uuid "c5ec945e-3519-52f9-be9c-a0a7c5e0668f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)=-{u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)={u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327995/selection/0713c2ccbbe11e7daafc1689c5a19dc8a5c6d940fdc603bf32ce386ad2fcc884" :answer/id #uuid "118cf61b-e642-5edb-a89c-b2880d26eb9d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)={u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)={u}_{1}(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327995/selection/d7ca297b82eb629b65a6baab347152601a24ce9dff8d624c9014923f1a3dcda5" :answer/id #uuid "ab6f4873-ea57-5609-acea-4d14129ab843" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)=-{u}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)={u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327995/selection/29af3c8e2052b94c83eb097cb4d214f75e81f9390df695b5868038ff4ce742b6" :answer/id #uuid "e77ddda6-34a0-5cf6-917c-e57aacfccf3c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)={u}_{1}(t)-{u}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)=-{u}_{1}(t)\\end{aligned}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-327995/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "5ee402a1-e0a2-5ca9-abc4-4a19a26a6f61" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-327995/selection/d7ca297b82eb629b65a6baab347152601a24ce9dff8d624c9014923f1a3dcda5" :answer-field/choices ["q-327995/selection/ea592d2b5df637fe876c4088b48c3bd8c43a23710531534f1b801de5b7751ea3" "q-327995/selection/fd562ba3a6d9d1e8c9739c1ce8f9fc0339e036fa8ea4ccfedc638fcf9b06c956" "q-327995/selection/0713c2ccbbe11e7daafc1689c5a19dc8a5c6d940fdc603bf32ce386ad2fcc884" "q-327995/selection/d7ca297b82eb629b65a6baab347152601a24ce9dff8d624c9014923f1a3dcda5" "q-327995/selection/29af3c8e2052b94c83eb097cb4d214f75e81f9390df695b5868038ff4ce742b6"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-327995" :question/id #uuid "b130cbca-fb25-5b40-a5cd-8a57800c8968" :question/math-academy-id "q-327995" :question/problem "Find the substitution that will decouple the following system of differential equations: \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=2{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-3{x}_{1}(t)-{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- Since $A$ is lower-triangular, the eigenvalues are \n\n$$\n{\\lambda }_{1}=2\\,\\text{and}\\,{\\lambda }_{2}=-1.\n$$\n\n- Let's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors.\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{1}=2,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{1}I=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ -3 & -3\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\n- For ${\\lambda }_{2}=-1,$ we get \n\n$$\nA-{\\lambda }_{2}I=[\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 0\\end{aligned}]∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n${v}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nTherefore, we have $E=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}].$\n\nFinally, the change of variables that decouples the system is given by $x(t)=Eu(t)$, or equivalently,\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)=-{u}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)={u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-327995/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2a962d5e-5cc9-530e-9f95-85c399af7e4b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-327995"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5974"] :question/problem "Let ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067055/assets/72d318ad7ca3ea0dff8b598a3c7126fd48a48f25fb6bdfec859e91701ffb9d15.png) and ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067055/assets/75c63b77244e0233dd11874e55a1ab674f6149d49b8fdd3c939afa1cf016ca6e.png) be eigenvectors of a matrix $A$ that correspond to eigenvalues $\\lambda_1=-1$ and $\\lambda_2=2,$ respectively.\nWhat is the general solution of the matrix differential equation $\\mathbf{x}'(t)=A\\mathbf{x}(t)?$" :question/worked-solution "Given a system of first-order linear ODEs in the form\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}'(t)=A\\mathbf{x}(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ has two distinct eigenvalues ${\\color{red}\\lambda_1}, {\\color{blue}\\lambda_2}$ with corresponding eigenvectors ${\\color{red}\\mathbf{v}_1}$ and ${\\color{blue}\\mathbf{v}_2},$ the formula for the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = c_1{\\color{red}\\mathbf{v}_1} e^{{\\color{red}\\lambda_1} t} + c_2{\\color{blue}\\mathbf{v}_2} e^{{\\color{blue}\\lambda_2} t}, \\qquad c_1,c_2 \\in \\mathbb{R}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution of our matrix differential equation is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}]{e}^{2t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5606"] :question/problem "Find the general solution to the system of differential equations \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=6{x}_{1}(t)+7{x}_{2}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-3{x}_{1}(t)-4{x}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n*Hint: The eigenvalues of the system's matrix are $\\lambda_1=-1$ and $\\lambda_2=3.$*" :question/worked-solution "First, we write down the matrix differential equation $\\mathbf{x}'(t)=A\\mathbf{x}(t)$ for the given system:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067055/assets/39f5b156a53392174c4b0c490f01c7bb3fee6530fc5f1e2e16be43d0de99067b.png)\n\nWe need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A.$\n\n- We are given that the eigenvalues are \n\n$$\n\\lambda_1=-1\n\\qquad\\text{and}\\qquad\n\\lambda_2=3.\n$$\n\n- Let's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors.\n\n- For $\\lambda_1 =-1,$ we get \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067055/assets/62cc97bb07ba88adc4b9fc6b42f33c924bf8d1d38c38ecf29973264c6ac24ee2.png)\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067055/assets/96afd68567ff82d1a461ad2b38f9492f644982f7dc4628526945bd619335c5ff.png)\n\n- For $\\lambda_2 =3,$ we get \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067055/assets/27f4874dc20e09331a89c5135dcacff5d6cce93d6040fdac954845478324b58b.png)\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067055/assets/6d3732ee67364278140c7e9ba5ec791cef69f4a60c8533d1f528c4bb5e718a35.png)\n\nThus, the general solution to the given system is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={c}_{1}{v}_{1}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{1}t}+{c}_{2}{v}_{2}{e}^{{\\lambda }_{2}t} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]{e}^{-t}+{c}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]{e}^{3t},\\,{c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "e-5605"] :question/problem "Find the substitution that will decouple the following system of differential equations: \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t)=-3{x}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t)=-3{x}_{1}(t)+{x}_{2}(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's construct the matrix differential equation $\\mathbf{x}'(t)=A\\mathbf{x}(t)$ for the given system:\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067055/assets/cd09988206ce7738d335cf25814f9820d5003c286904c8e136e55724f2fc1185.png)\n\nWe need to find the eigenvalues and the eigenvectors of the matrix $A.$\n\n- Since $A$ is lower-triangular, the eigenvalues are \n\n$$\n\\lambda_1=-3\n\\qquad\\text{and}\\qquad\n\\lambda_2=1.\n$$\n\n- Let's go through the process of finding the eigenvectors.\n\n- For $\\lambda_1 =-3,$ we get \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067055/assets/9bd0bffeaccd9f7523829b9f385c5e75a25ecd663877f0b5711d271938e484e6.png)\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067055/assets/0683c697abc42c91bc62d5f52aafa1fd7b79cd5156e999b3aac4802d9359773e.png)\n\n- For $\\lambda_2 =1,$ we get \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067055/assets/816a9a9b4948cae2d5a21b6e5ccf80928cadefb4d8a7ca1d333166b2fe66e5ac.png)\nSo, we get an eigenvector \n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067055/assets/491ab9ee9c59586dbccb6c043a3225adc3ef95496c056d37891594513f1f6069.png)\n\nTherefore, we have ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14067055/assets/6c51e641ebd7c4e64366c23aa9c7e091c3b711724069b47b104dc6f1c588f7bc.png)\n\nFinally, the change of variables that decouples the system is given by $\\mathbf{x}(t) = E\\mathbf{u}(t),$ or equivalently,\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t)=4{u}_{1}(t) \\\\ {x}_{2}(t)=3{u}_{1}(t)+{u}_{2}(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
